  "Question": "Which quantity involving the distances from a moving point to two foci is used in the definition of a hyperbola?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Their sum",
    "B": "The absolute value of their difference",
    "C": "Their product",
    "D": "Their quotient"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "For a hyperbola, the absolute value of the difference between the distances is constant; for an ellipse, the sum of the distances is constant.",
